   "type": "h1",
   "text": "3. Contar una historia"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "<i>Last Saturday I <b>got</b> up late. I <b>had</b> breakfast and then I <b>went</b> to the market. I <b>bought</b> some fruit and I <b>met</b> an old friend. We <b>drank</b> a coffee and we <b>spoke</b> for an hour. In the evening I <b>was</b> very tired, so I <b>went</b> to bed early.</i>"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "dutch",
   "title": "become y get = hacerse, ponerse",
   "text": "El español tiene muchos verbos para un cambio: hacerse, ponerse, volverse, llegar a ser. El inglés usa sobre todo <b>become</b> y <b>get</b>: <i>She became a doctor</i> = Se hizo médica; <i>It got dark</i> = Se hizo de noche; <i>He got angry</i> = Se enfadó."
  },
